Excerpt of meeting minutes (2026-10-05 10:00-10:40, small meeting room on the 2nd floor of the S-750 Biology Building)
Topic: Safety review of the preparation protocol for CS-007249 phosphorus-32-labeled probe
Attendees: radiation protection specialist, 2 members of the research group, equipment administrator; another 3 people were on leave.
Summary of conclusions:
1. This protocol uses phosphorus-32-labeled dCTP, with a single-order activity of 18.5 MBq and a cumulative total of 6 batches for the year;
2. The operation is performed on a benchtop in an ordinary molecular laboratory, with no lead glass shielding configured, and the operator does not wear a personal dosimeter;
3. Radioactive liquid waste is temporarily stored for 10 half-lives and then handed over to a qualified unit for disposal;
4. The protocol contains no biological materials and no flammable or explosive chemicals.
According to the radiation safety scoring table: activity not lower than 10 MBq is scored 2 points, no shielding is scored 1 point, no personal dose monitoring is scored 1 point, totaling 4 points; 4 points or above on this table is extremely high.
Other matters: The temperature recorder DEV-7164 in the third-floor cold storage room alarmed at 23:10 yesterday, which is unrelated to this topic; a separate work order TK-20261024-2532 has been opened for handling; the sample transport temperature control issue asked about by a logistics dispatcher by phone is postponed to the next meeting.

Excerpt of the meeting minutes No. CS-007250 of the Safety Committee pre-review meeting
Time: 2026-10-12 14:30—15:20 Venue: Small meeting room on the third floor at S-826
Agenda item: re-review application for the lentiviral packaging and transduction experimental protocol for batch B-56425 (protocol number LP-SO-20260901-727516)
Key points:
1) The protocol uses a third-generation lentiviral vector, with HEK293T packaging cells, a target titer of 5×10^7 TU/mL, followed by transduction of primary neurons; it involves 4 centrifugation steps per batch with aerosol risk, all performed in sealed centrifuge cups;
2) All operations are performed in a BSL-2 biosafety cabinet; 2 personnel are involved, both have been vaccinated as appropriate and have completed 8 hours of biosafety training;
3) Waste is treated as infectious waste and autoclaved at 121 ℃ for 30 minutes;
4) The protocol does not involve radionuclides; the only organic solvent is 200 mL of isopropanol used for surface disinfection, and there is no live electrical work above 36 V.
Scoring: According to the Detailed Rules for Hazard Classification of Experimental Protocols, the biological dimension is 2 points (replication-defective viral vector + BSL-2 operations), chemical 0 points, radiological 0 points, electrical 0 points, cumulative 2 points. The detailed rules stipulate that a cumulative score of 0 is low, 1 is medium, 2—3 is high, and 4 or above is extremely high; and a cumulative score ≥2 must be submitted to the Safety Committee for re-review. The conclusion is implemented accordingly.
Note: The temperature control probe of the incubator on the third floor at S-532, reported for repair last week, was replaced on 2026-09-10; this is unrelated to this agenda item and is for reference only.
